<resources>
    <!--
      ★ Window background = opaque black (final decision 2026-09-13)

      Why `windowIsTranslucent=true` **must not** be used:
      measured (by comparing screenshots) that as soon as the window is translucent, **the launcher's / other apps'
      icons and text behind it show through completely** and blend with the dashboard into a "mixed" mess — that is not
      the "transparency" the user wanted.

      On AR glasses the correct implementation of "transparent" is **opaque black**:
      black pixels emit no light → the wearer sees the real world (equivalent to seeing through),
      while **the app behind is blocked out**, so the dashboard can float cleanly in view.
      This is also the intent of "does not block the field of view" in `activity_main.xml`.

      (The panel itself still has **no background colour**: only text and status dots.)
    -->
    <style name="Theme.RokidGlasses" parent="Theme.AppCompat.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowContentOverlay">@null</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>
